WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.500
Your SAP data is in Fabric. Hundreds of tables with short, cryptic names.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.000
How do they connect?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.600
Krusgraph finds the links between your tables.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.600
Order lines to orders, orders to customers, then deliveries and invoices.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.100
Krusgraph checks them against your rows: 32 of 34 links hold.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.600
Then Krusgraph suggests data products: Order to cash, and Customer master.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.100
Each with its tables in plain words, and an owner you choose.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.800
Krusgraph builds the semantic model from Order to cash.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.600
Facts and dimensions snap together, and every total counts each order once.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.700
Then a report on that model: order value, top customers, billing.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.200
From SAP tables to a report you can trust.
